notes.body:
Two possibilities here. The smaller change from what you have:

```suggestion:-2+0
    uint32_t *key = wmem_new(wmem_file_scope(), uint32_t);
    *key = entityid;
    packet_context_t *context = wmem_map_lookup(packet_context_map, key);
```

If the key will always fit in a `uint32_t` then you can instead do this to reduce the amount of mallocs needed:

```suggestion:-2+0
    packet_context_t *context = wmem_map_lookup(packet_context_map, GUINT_TO_POINTER(entityid));
```

Note that your choice here (and below) will affect your call to `wmem_map_new_autoreset()` as I'll note there.

suggestions.from_content:
guint32 *key = g_new(guint32, 1);
*key = entityid;
packet_context_t *context = g_hash_table_lookup(packet_context_map, key);

suggestions.to_content:
uint32_t *key = wmem_new(wmem_file_scope(), uint32_t);
*key = entityid;
packet_context_t *context = wmem_map_lookup(packet_context_map, key);

